            <ArticleTitle>Imaging of the thoracic aorta.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e391-412</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.lpm.2011.03.017</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Three-dimensional vascular imaging techniques offer a significant advantage over traditional imaging techniques. Spatial resolution of current state-of-the-art allows sufficient depiction of anatomical detail. Pre-operative planning of complex endovascular procedures is facilitated by state-of-the-art imaging. Cone-beam CT holds great promise in guiding complex endovascular procedures.</AbstractText>
